"P-Stratum common exposes at most one active Edge per authenticated Peer Node identity in one Interface instance."},{"id":"PR-INV-004","statement":"Every Edge snapshot contains at least one service profile and one Obfuscated degree value."},{"id":"PR-INV-005","statement":"Obfuscated degree is interpreted only as a privacy-preserving neighbor-expansion cardinality."},{"id":"PR-INV-006","statement":"Every accepted Submission receives exactly one terminal completion event, including before an Interface reset terminates the instance."},{"id":"PR-INV-007","statement":"No SDU is delivered after edge-removed for the same Edge incarnation."},{"id":"PR-INV-008","statement":"The baseline service preserves complete SDU boundaries and provides no inter-SDU ordering guarantee."},{"id":"PR-INV-009","statement":"Queues are finite and backpressure is observable without polling."},{"id":"PR-INV-010","statement":"The initial Edge snapshot and event stream form one atomic, monotonically sequenced history."},{"id":"PR-INV-011","statement":"Runtime identifiers are local to one Interface instance and invalid after close or reset."},{"id":"PR-INV-012","statement":"An Edge identifier is never reused within one Interface instance."},{"id":"PR-INV-013","statement":"A PeerHandle is stable for one NodeIdentityId within an Interface instance and is never assigned to a different identity."},{"id":"PR-INV-014","statement":"Every Obfuscated degree profile used by an Edge is declared when the Interface opens, and its value stays within the declared bound."},{"id":"PR-INV-015","statement":"Mandatory version semantics are not negotiated as optional capabilities."},{"id":"PR-INV-016","statement":"An Edge snapshot carried by an event belongs to the same Interface instance as the event context."},{"id":"PR-INV-017","statement":"The provider reserves capacity for the terminal reset event and never silently drops events while the Interface remains open."}],"limits":[{"id":1,"name":"MAXIMUM_EDGE_COUNT"},{"